Third-party components and models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains NO third-party source code: the runtime uses only the
Python standard library. The components below are external dependencies that a
user installs and runs themselves. They are NOT redistributed here, and they are
NOT covered by the Apache License above.

1. Gemma (Google)

   The application sends prompts to a Gemma model served locally by Ollama.
   Gemma is not open source and is not licensed under Apache-2.0. Its use is
   governed by the Gemma Terms of Use and the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy:

       https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
       https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy

   Those terms include a flow-down obligation: anyone who redistributes Gemma,
   or a model derived from it, must pass the same use restrictions on to their
   own recipients. This project distributes neither Gemma nor any derivative of
   it — it only calls a model that the user has obtained and installed. Anyone
   deploying this project for others remains responsible for complying with
   those terms.

2. Ollama

   Model runtime, MIT License. https://github.com/ollama/ollama

3. SerpApi (optional)

   Live rule verification and claim-channel lookup use the SerpApi service when
   a key is configured. Commercial service under its own terms; no key is
   distributed with this repository. Without a key, the application degrades to
   an explicit offline mode rather than failing.

4. FFmpeg (optional)

   Used to convert browser audio recordings and WEBP documents before they are
   passed to the model. LGPL/GPL depending on build; invoked as an external
   process, never linked or redistributed.

5. Poppler (optional)

   Used via `pdftoppm` to render the first page of a PDF. GPL-2.0; invoked as an
   external process, never linked or redistributed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files under `knowledge/airline_policies/` summarise publicly documented claim
procedures. Each record carries the official source URL and a verification date.
They are short factual summaries, not copies of the source pages. Airline names
and trademarks belong to their respective owners and are used here only to
identify the procedure being described.

The demonstration document `billet_avion_fictif.*` is fictitious. "Aurora
Airlines" is an invented carrier and does not designate any real company.

